section R05Seg10
/-!
# VIII08 — odd magnetic potential / arbitrary rotation: existence, uniqueness, stability

Anchor `(R_h, R_i, Q) = (3, 1, 3/2)`, `I = (3, ∞)`.  For arbitrary `j : ℝ` and `q, r ∈ C¹(U)`
with `U = (-1/12, 5/12)`, `K = [0, 1/3]`, `s(x) = 3j + q(x)`:

* `b_s` solves the ACTUAL equation `Lmag b = s(1/R)/R³` on all of `I`, with `MagClass 3`;
* the rotation `v = ∫₀^{1/R} t(2j + 6 b_s(1/t) - t r(t)) dt` solves `Dell[j, b_s, v] = r(1/R)/R`
  on all of `I`, with `VClass 3`;
* the sharp bounds `|R b_s| ≤ B/8`, `|R² b_s'| ≤ B`, `|R³(v - j/R²)| ≤ B/4 + Ar/3`,
  `|R⁴(v' + 2j/R³)| ≤ 3B/4 + Ar`, `B = 3|j| + Aq`, hold on all of `I`;
* the solutions are unique in their classes (same-source uniqueness), and
  `R b_s → sigma_b = -[∫₀^a Ac(t) s(t) dt]/(2 A0)`, `R² v → j`,
  `R³(v - j/R²) → 2 sigma_b - r(0)/3`, `R⁴(v' + 2j/R³) → r(0) - 6 sigma_b`.

`A0 = lim_{R→∞} aY(R) = sSup (aY '' I)` is a real number with `1/3 ≤ A0 ≤ 27/16`.
-/

